## CRITICAL RULES

### Extraction Method
- **REQUIRED:** Read EACH XML file directly using the Read tool
- **REQUIRED:** Extract EVERY attribute (`position`, `cacheEnabled`, `mode`, `allowSimultaneous`)
- **FORBIDDEN:** Using Python/Bash scripts for XML extraction (misses nested details)

### RGV Loop — Read-Generate-Verify (CRITICAL)

Every section in Phases 1-4 MUST follow the RGV loop. Defined ONCE in `@01_Guidance.mdc §1`:

```
FOR EACH section to generate:
  1. RE-READ  — Fresh Read tool call on ALL relevant XML files for this section
  2. INVENTORY — Count target elements in XML, list names, COMMIT to count N
  3. GENERATE — Produce section content (must contain exactly N items)
  4. VERIFY  — Count generated items, compare to N
  5. FIX     — If mismatch → RE-READ XML, find missing, fix BEFORE proceeding
  6. CHECKPOINT — Emit micro-checkpoint with counts, write to file, proceed
```

**Why:** Each section is an **ATOMIC UNIT**. The agent must not start section N+1 until section N passes verification. This prevents summarization — the root cause of missed mapping fields.

### Output Separation (CRITICAL)
- **Verification counts** (Shape Count, Mapping Count) belong ONLY in `supporting-docs/verification-checklist.md`
- **NEVER** place count verification blocks in the main document
- **ALL** field mapping rows must appear in the main document — NEVER summarize or abbreviate
- Detailed shape configs → `supporting-docs/shape-configuration.md`
- Detailed profiles → `supporting-docs/profile-structures.md`

### Zero Assumptions
- Document exactly what XML contains — no inference, no external knowledge
- Extract ALL fields (mapped AND unmapped) from profiles
- Include COMPLETE script/Groovy code — never truncate

---

## MANDATORY BEHAVIOR

- **Continuous processing** — process all 6 phases automatically, never ask "Should I continue?"
- **RGV enforcement** — every section must pass Read → Inventory → Generate → Verify before proceeding
- **Micro-checkpoints** — emit count-verified checkpoint after EVERY section (e.g., `✅ 4.1: MapName — 22/22 mappings`)
- **Progressive file writing** — write to files after each section completion
- **Template compliance** — read `templates/documentation-style.yaml` and examples BEFORE output
- **ALWAYS** produce `<thinking>` block before each phase/section output
- **ALWAYS** flag assumptions with ⚠️ ASSUMPTION marker
- **ALWAYS** cite XML source file and element for every extraction
- See `@02_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc` for full anti-pattern list

